bottled-judge
=============

Owner-defined contests have problems, hidden tests, limits and hacking
phases. Successful hacks test every accepted solution to that problem.
Contestant labels are unauthenticated.

The judge runs on Debian 13 with Python 3.13.5, OCaml 5.3,
GCC/g++ 14.2 (C23/C++23) and Rust 1.85 (edition 2024).
Only image packages are available. Dependencies cannot be downloaded.

Per-test CPU limits are 100-10000 ms and memory settings are 32-1024 MB.
Runs also have a wall timeout and 64 MiB output limit. Builds have
separate 30 s and 2 GiB limits. Submissions run unprivileged without
network access, with process limits and cleanup. This setup is for
semi-trusted users only. Do not run untrusted code without stronger isolation.

